course: dictionary
lesson: 9866
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The words around a word, its context, tell you which meaning the writer means. «The bird used its syrinx to sing.» Birds sing, so syrinx here must be the part of a bird that makes its song.
explain: Syrinx is a noun with three meanings: a bird's voice organ, a set of panpipes, and a nymph in a Greek myth. Look for clue words. Words like bird, sing or chest point to the first meaning. Words like music, pipes or reeds point to the second. Words like nymph, myth or Pan point to the third.
explain: Always check your choice by swapping it into the sentence. «In one myth a nymph called Syrinx ran from Pan and was turned into reeds.» A nymph cannot be a set of pipes, so this is the Greek myth meaning. If your meaning does not fit, try the next one.
fact: Syrinx is a noun, and it has three meanings.
fact: In science, the syrinx is the voice organ of a bird, deep in its chest where the windpipe splits.
fact: A syrinx is also a set of panpipes, a simple instrument of reed tubes of different lengths that you blow across.
fact: In Greek myth, Syrinx was a nymph who ran from the god Pan and was turned into reeds, which Pan made into pipes.
fact: Birds sing with a syrinx, not with vocal cords like people.
exercise: «In science lessons, birds sing with the syrinx, not with vocal cords like people.» What is the syrinx here? | A set of panpipes | A type of reed | A nymph from a Greek myth | *The voice organ of a bird
exercise: «In one myth a nymph called Syrinx ran from Pan and was turned into reeds.» Which meaning of syrinx is this? | A kind of songbird | *A nymph from a Greek myth | A set of panpipes | A bird's voice organ
exercise: «In The Wind in the Willows, Rat and Mole hear the music of Pan's pipes on an island.» What does syrinx mean if it is the pipes? | *A set of panpipes made from reed tubes | A nymph who ran away | The windpipe of a bird | A bird's voice organ, deep in its chest
test: «The robin used its syrinx to sing a sweet song all morning.» Which meaning fits best? | A Greek nymph | A set of panpipes | *The voice organ of a bird | A type of reed
test: Lily says a syrinx is a kind of bird. What should you tell her? | Yes, it is a small songbird | Yes, it is a kind of owl | No, it is a bird's nest | *No, it is the voice organ deep in a bird's chest, and it can also mean panpipes
exam: Which sentence uses syrinx to mean a nymph? | The syrinx is deep in the chest | Pan played the syrinx on the hill | *In one myth, a nymph called Syrinx ran from Pan | The bird used its syrinx to sing
